                         QUARTERLY FIELD REPORT
                         Marchmont Survey Group

     The  autumn  survey  of  the  eastern  parcels  concluded  on
     the  fourteenth.   Weather  held  for  six  of  the  nine days
     scheduled,  which  is  better  than  the  spring  season  and
     considerably better than last autumn.

     Three  parcels  required  re-measurement.   The  discrepancy
     in  each  case  traced  back  to  the  1971  reference  stake,
     which  has  moved  or  been  moved.   A  new  datum  point  is
     recommended before the spring season opens.
